  "question": {
    "text": "Combustion of Hydrogen in a fuel cell at <math> <mrow> <mn>300</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>K</mtext></mrow> </math> is represented as&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mfenced> <mtext>g</mtext> </mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mfenced> <mtext>g</mtext> </mfenced><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mtext>O</mtext><mfenced> <mtext>g</mtext> </mfenced></mrow> <mo>.</mo></math><br />\rIf <math><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> and <math><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></math> are <math><mo>-</mo><mn>241.60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mo>-</mo><mn>228.40</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> are respectively for&nbsp;<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp; then the value of <math><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> for the above process is",
